{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# The step-budget repetition diagnostic is computed, then dropped\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered while root-causing [rebar:bf31-fd55-d28d-4b7a]. The reported symptom was \"the gate cannot\nbe tuned because it cannot be observed\" — no partial verdict, no count of anything, just a bare\nbudget number. The diagnostic that answers it **already exists** and is thrown away one frame from\nthe surface.\n\n`interpret_failure` (`src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py:75-103`) builds `budget_diag` via\n`usage_log.failure_usage`, which reduces every tool call to a `(tool_name, sha256(args)[:8])`\nsignature and summarizes it — `tool_calls_distinct`, `max_consecutive_repeat`,\n`top_repeated_tool_calls`. That is precisely the loop-vs-explore discriminator, and it is attached\nas `budget_err.diagnostic`.\n\nIt then goes nowhere. `emit_gate_error` is only called by `raise_completion_workflow_failure` when\n`failure_diagnostic` is truthy (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:373-403`), and\n`failure_diagnostic` is set ONLY inside `CompletionAgentStep._recover` — which a budget exhaustion\nnever reaches (the sibling [rebar:fd84-92b4-01ba-4911] fixes reachability). So **no `gate_error_v1`\nsidecar is written** and the CLI message carries none of it. In the instrumented reproduction the\npropagated exception reached the caller with `diagnostic: null`.\n\nTwo operators burned ~50 minutes each escalating the budget 480 -> 1600 against a constraint that\nwas never a budget (and ticket 46a2-9c1a-d855-4706 records a third: 480 -> 1200, same result). The\nmeasurement that would have said so in one line was computed on the first run and discarded.\n\n## Approach\n\nWire the already-computed diagnostic through the two drops. First, `CompletionAgentStep` records the\ncaught exception's `.diagnostic` onto `self.failure_diagnostic` when it enters recovery (fd84 adds\nthe budget entry edge; this ticket makes the diagnostic it carries survive), so\n`raise_completion_workflow_failure` — whose sidecar emission and `CompletionRecoveryError` path\nalready exist and are keyed on a truthy `failure_diagnostic` — emits the `gate_error_v1` sidecar\ncarrying the repetition counters. Second, the operator-facing close-gate failure message renders the\ndistinct-vs-total counts (via the existing `usage_log.format_repetition` renderer, which already\nformats exactly these fields) so \"it looped\" is distinguishable from \"it ran out of room\" without\nreading a log. No new computation, no new fields: every value is already produced by\n`usage_log.failure_usage`; this ticket only stops dropping it.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py` — set `failure_diagnostic` from the caught\n  exception's diagnostic; include the repetition summary in the message\n  `raise_completion_workflow_failure` raises.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_token_recovery.py` — the tests below.\n\nOut of scope: making budget exhaustion reach this code at all ([rebar:fd84-92b4-01ba-4911], a\ndeclared dependency); the detector's new field ([rebar:70bc-ab05-6d4c-45a0] — whatever fields\n`failure_usage` produces are carried, so the new field flows through automatically once 70bc lands).\n\n## Testing\n\n    pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_token_recovery.py -q\n\nHappy path: a budget exhaustion whose recovery also fails emits a `gate_error_v1` sidecar populated\nwith the repetition counters. Edge: a failure with NO diagnostic (the pre-existing bare path) still\nraises `LLMError` exactly as today (regression-pinned). Privacy: the sidecar payload carries no\nprompts, tool arguments, or response text.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a step-budget exhaustion whose recovery also fails writes a `gate_error_v1` sidecar carrying\n      the repetition summary (`requests`, `tool_calls`, `tool_calls_distinct`,\n      `max_consecutive_repeat`, `top_repeated_tool_calls`); verified by a test asserting the sidecar\n      is emitted and its counters are populated\n- [ ] the operator-facing close-gate failure message includes the distinct-vs-total tool-call counts,\n      so \"it looped\" is distinguishable from \"it ran out of room\" without reading a log; verified by\n      a test asserting the raised error's message contains the counts\n- [ ] the sidecar payload stays free of prompts, tool arguments and response text (the existing\n      privacy contract in `usage_log.failure_usage` is preserved); verified by a test asserting only\n      hashed signatures and counters appear\n- [ ] a failure without any diagnostic still raises the current bare `LLMError` unchanged (no\n      manufactured empty sidecar); regression-pinned by a test"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785955019122906001,"uuid":"d9925e31-f5d2-4a0a-ba11-83c447000fb8"}